const tasks=[{day:'DAY 01',title:'Trust the data',items:[['Download and inventory the official Bot-IoT 5% subset','A'],['Inspect labels, schema, missing values, and imbalance','A'],['Create the shared configuration and smoke-test runner','B']]},{day:'DAY 02',title:'Compare the bench',items:[['Freeze one shared train / validation / test split','A + B'],['Train all five models on the same sample','A + B'],['Generate metrics and confusion matrices','A']]},{day:'DAY 03',title:'Package the proof',items:[['Benchmark CPU latency, size, and memory','B'],['Run the save / load prediction demo','B'],['Finish the report and rehearse the demo','A + B']]}];
const models=[['01','Decision Tree','A cheap, interpretable baseline.','Small artifact · explainable'],['02','Random Forest','A stronger nonlinear baseline.','Accuracy vs. size tradeoff'],['03','Logistic Regression','A compact linear reference.','Fast · easy to deploy'],['04','XGBoost','The boosted-tree contender.','Strong tabular performance'],['05','Dense Network','A small neural comparison.','64 → 32 → K · CPU-first']];
const prompts=[['SHARED CONTEXT','Shared context for every agent','Both','You are assisting a two-person academic IoT intrusion-detection mini-project with a three-day deadline. Hardware: Windows, 8 GB RAM, CPU-only execution. Follow IoT_Project_Plan_3_Days.txt. Dataset: the official Bot-IoT 5% subset, whose actual files and schema must be inspected. Required models: Decision Tree, Random Forest, Logistic Regression, XGBoost, and a small dense neural network. Use one frozen train/validation/test split and the same training sample. Never fit preprocessing on validation/test, expose labels or metadata as features, invent dataset columns, fabricate metrics, or tune on final test results. Keep memory bounded and train one model at a time. First inspect the repository and existing instructions. State your assumptions, implement only the assigned module, run targeted checks, and summarize changed files, commands, actual outputs, and remaining issues. If data is missing, report the missing input rather than presenting synthetic results as real experiments. Coordinate shared interface changes before altering them.'],['SETUP','Establish the project skeleton','B','Using the shared context, create a minimal Python project structure and requirements.in. Add YAML configuration for paths, seed=42, model parameters, thread budgets, and output locations. Implement common configuration loading, reproducible run IDs, and result metadata. Document PowerShell commands using .venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe directly. Do not download the dataset, install GPU dependencies, or create a dashboard. Coordinate feature_schema.json, label_map.json, and the evaluation interface with Person A. Use synthetic fixtures only for code smoke tests and label them clearly. Deliver a short README with commands and a list of interfaces still to be implemented.'],['DATA','Prepare and audit the data','A','Using the shared context, inspect the actual CSV headers and official feature documentation before coding mappings. Implement src/prepare_data.py for chunked or disk-backed processing. Produce a source manifest, feature exclusions with reasons, real label counts, missing-value statistics, canonical feature fingerprints, duplicate/conflicting-label audits, frozen splits, and a reproducible reduced training sample. Prefer verified capture/session/time separation when feasible; otherwise document a deduplicated stratified row split and its correlation limitation. Do not assume CSV partitions are independent captures. Preserve holdout prevalence, evaluate in batches, and assert no row/fingerprint overlap. Report rare classes with inadequate split support. Save schemas and manifests that every model can reuse. Never guess unknown labels or include target fields in X.'],['MODELS','Implement XGBoost and the dense network','B','Using the shared context, implement src/train_xgb.py and src/train_dense.py with the exact same split and training sample as the baselines. Use CPU XGBoost histogram training and a PyTorch input-64-32-K network with ReLU hidden layers, raw output logits, CrossEntropyLoss, Adam, batch size 256, at most 20 epochs, and external-validation macro-F1 early stopping with patience 3. Save and restore the best checkpoint. Use training-derived class/sample weights only when justified and log them; do not use binary scale_pos_weight as multiclass weighting. Keep Windows DataLoader workers at zero. Save preprocessing, label order, architecture, and state_dict. Verify loading in a fresh process and prediction parity. Do not silently swap the shared validation split for an internal one.'],['EVAL','Evaluate and analyze errors','A','Using the shared context, implement a common evaluator for all saved models. Stream held-out batches, calculate per-class precision/recall/F1/support, macro and weighted summaries, accuracy, binary attack recall, and benign false-positive rate. Use the saved class order consistently. Generate raw and row-normalized confusion matrices and model_comparison.csv. Report zero-support classes and undefined metrics honestly. Identify the largest off-diagonal errors by count and rate, and keep false negatives separate from attack-category confusions. Do not modify a model or choose thresholds based on test results. Produce observations only from actual outputs and link each table or plot to its run metadata.'],['BENCH','Benchmark inference','B','Using the shared context, implement src/predict.py and src/benchmark.py. Validate feature schemas and use trusted saved preprocessing/model bundles. Benchmark one model per fresh process on the same laptop and fixed validation-derived input sample. Limit threads consistently, warm up 100 calls, time at least 1000 single-row predictions, repeat three times, and report p50/p95. Measure batch-256 throughput separately. Time model-only and preprocessing-plus-model inference separately; exclude disk I/O and training. Record load time, CPU/OS/runtime versions, bundle size, baseline RSS, sampled peak RSS, and sampling interval. State that packet capture, feature extraction, and actual edge-device performance are unmeasured. Check prediction parity after serialization and return generated CSV files, not guessed timings.']];
const $=s=>document.querySelector(s),$$=s=>[...document.querySelectorAll(s)];let checked=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('iot-plan-tasks')||'[]');
function renderTasks(){let total=0;$('#timeline').innerHTML=tasks.map((d,di)=>'<article class="day-card"><div class="day-top"><div><div class="day-kicker">'+d.day+'</div><h3>'+d.title+'</h3></div><div class="day-num">0'+(di+1)+'</div></div>'+d.items.map((it,ii)=>{let id=di+'-'+ii,ok=checked.includes(id);total++;return '<div class="task '+(ok?'done':'')+'"><input type="checkbox" id="'+id+'" data-id="'+id+'" '+(ok?'checked':'')+'><label for="'+id+'">'+it[0]+'<span class="task-owner">Owner · '+it[1]+'</span></label></div>'}).join('')+'</article>').join('');$$('.task input').forEach(i=>i.onchange=()=>{let id=i.dataset.id;checked=i.checked?[...new Set([...checked,id])]:checked.filter(x=>x!==id);localStorage.setItem('iot-plan-tasks',JSON.stringify(checked));renderTasks()});$('#progressText').textContent=checked.length+' / '+total+' tasks';$('#progressBar').style.width=checked.length/total*100+'%'}
function renderModels(){const show=i=>{let m=models[i];$$('.model-card').forEach((x,j)=>x.classList.toggle('active',j===i));$('#modelDetail').innerHTML='<strong>'+m[1]+'</strong><span>'+m[3]+'. Train with the shared frozen split, then compare macro-F1, minority recall, benign false-positive rate, artifact size, and p95 CPU latency.</span>'};$('#modelGrid').innerHTML=models.map((m,i)=>'<button class="model-card '+(i?'':'active')+'" data-model="'+i+'"><span class="model-index">'+m[0]+'</span><h3>'+m[1]+'</h3><p>'+m[2]+'</p></button>').join('');$$('.model-card').forEach(x=>x.onclick=()=>show(+x.dataset.model));show(0)}
function renderChecklist(){let items=['Python 3.11 or 3.12 · 64-bit','Git for Windows + VS Code','Core ML packages + CPU PyTorch','pip check passes · imports verified'];let saved=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('iot-checks')||'[]');$('#checklist').innerHTML=items.map((x,i)=>'<label class="check-item"><input type="checkbox" data-check="'+i+'" '+(saved.includes(String(i))?'checked':'')+'><span>'+x+'</span></label>').join('');$$('[data-check]').forEach(x=>x.onchange=()=>localStorage.setItem('iot-checks',JSON.stringify($$('[data-check]:checked').map(y=>y.dataset.check))))}
let selected=0;function renderPrompts(){const show=i=>{selected=i;let p=prompts[i];$('#promptTag').textContent=p[0];$('#promptTitle').textContent=p[1];$('#promptBody').textContent=p[3];$('#promptOwner').textContent='Owner · '+p[2];$$('.prompt-tab').forEach((x,j)=>x.classList.toggle('active',j===i))};$('#promptList').innerHTML=prompts.map((p,i)=>'<button class="prompt-tab '+(i?'':'active')+'" data-prompt="'+i+'">'+p[0]+'<br><strong>'+p[1]+'</strong></button>').join('');$$('.prompt-tab').forEach(x=>x.onclick=()=>show(+x.dataset.prompt));show(0);const copy=()=>navigator.clipboard?.writeText(prompts[selected][3]);$('#copyPrompt').onclick=copy;$('#copyPromptBtn').onclick=copy}
function copyText(text,button){navigator.clipboard?.writeText(text);let old=button.textContent;button.textContent='Copied';setTimeout(()=>button.textContent=old,1300)}$('#copyInstall').onclick=e=>copyText('py -3.11 -m venv .venv\\n.\\\\.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe -m pip install --upgrade pip\\n.\\\\.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.in\\n.\\\\.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe -m pip install torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu\\n.\\\\.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe -m pip check',e.currentTarget);$('#themeToggle').onclick=()=>document.body.classList.toggle('dark');renderTasks();renderModels();renderChecklist();renderPrompts();
